**What the long run shows:**

- **It settles after about 2 minutes.** From run 6 onwards generation stayed within 56.3–56.6 tokens per second, and the temperature held at 80–82°C. **About 56.4 tokens per second is the card's sustained speed at 180 W.** That's about 5% below the first run and about 9% below a cool card at 250 W (62.63).
- **The 180 W limit doesn't keep the card much cooler over time.**
  - After 2 minutes it was at 77°C, but over the long run it kept climbing to **82°C**, only 2°C below the 250 W peak.
  - The fan stopped at 50% again, so the fan curve, not power, sets where the temperature ends up.
  - It never crossed into thermal throttling, though, so the power limit was the only thing holding it back.
- **Energy and speed both matched the earlier 180 W test.** It used about 3.9 kJ per run, the same as the 5-run 180 W test, and the first 5 runs were within 1% of it. The results are repeatable.

The 200 W setting hadn't taken effect because the Ollama service wasn't restarted after the limit was changed.

